{"text": "Amazon’s AWS share of revenue and its three-year trend could not be settled from the analyst evidence available in this turn: the issuer analyst returned no brief, so I do not have a filed revenue-mix figure to cite.

On the market side, AMZN’s return over the last year versus SPY was -8.12% [f_4a549c6d2bbb]. The one-year market-factor fit explains 27.8% [f_02268a2b5c2b] of AMZN’s return versus SPY; the fit is incomplete.

Implication for the book: the relative underperformance was only partly market-driven, so there is still a meaningful name-specific component. If the AWS mix had been rising over the last three years, that would matter for the business mix reading; if it had been falling, it would point the other way. I’d change the read only once the filed AWS revenue-share evidence is in hand.", "problems": [{"reason": "requirement_unaddressed"}, {"reason": "requirement_unaddressed"}]}
